# LA-7 stdin script — drive Alex to the stove.
#
# Format: each turn is a fenced ```python ... ``` block followed by a
# bare `EOF` line. The StdinClient reads one block per agent turn.
#
# Strategy:
# 1. Each turn enumerates what SAM3 has currently grounded so the
#    log shows which labels were seen and where.
# 2. Tries ``stove`` first, then ``oven`` (the kitchen appliance can
#    SAM3-label either way depending on prompt prioritisation).
# 3. ``goto`` is the only skill that actually drives the robot in
#    this build (peek / survey / face write bundle fields no
#    consumer reads yet). Once a goto fires, Phase 1-4's planner
#    walks Alex; the agent then waits — gating on FSM≠IDLE — until
#    arrival, at which point we declare success.
# 4. If we burn through every turn without finding the goal, the
#    last turn calls ``fail()`` so the run logs an honest failure
#    rather than masquerading as a success.

```python
# Turn 1
nodes = list_scene()["value"]
print("la7 turn 1 seen:", [(n["label"], n["world_xy"]) for n in nodes])
goto_done = False
for label in ("stove", "oven"):
    r = find(label)
    if r["status"] == "ok":
        goto(label)
        goto_done = True
        break
print("la7 turn 1 goto_done:", goto_done)
```
EOF

